# Both images build from the repo root, because pnpm workspace links mean the API
# and the dashboard cannot be built from their own directories alone — they need the
# lockfile, the workspace manifest, and packages/* as well.
#
# Everything listed here is excluded from the build context that gets sent to the
# daemon. Keeping node_modules out is not just about speed: the local copy holds
# Windows-resolved binaries (esbuild, pg), and copying those into a Linux image
# produces a container that fails at runtime in confusing ways. Each image installs
# its own dependencies for its own platform instead.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output is regenerated inside the image.
dist
**/dist
coverage
**/coverage

# Secrets. DATABASE_URL and three provider API keys live here; an image layer is
# forever and shipping one is how keys leak.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git
.github
.gitignore
*.log

# Not needed to build or run anything.
docs
README.md
**/*.md
